        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I miss `c-f` during `grn` (LSP rename). I used to `c-f` to jump to cmdwin to make edits in normal mode (e.g. renaming `authStatePath` to `playwrightAuthStatePath` in cmdwin was `Iplaywright<C-C>l~` but now requires me to delete and re-type the entire variable name or use `PageUp` or something similar to jump to front, since `C-A` is not supported in that `input`).\n\nI rarely use cmdwin for other purposes, so this change for now harms my workflow more than it adds eye candy :/",
