            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I noticed I can do `CTRL-W n` do open a new window. I suppose that should be disabled\n\nThat limitation was intentionally dropped: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40484\n\n> I did notice that I don't have all my mappings in that buffer, though\n\nyeah currently the child-nvim is [started with](https://github.com/justinmk/neovim/blob/e0dffc5f044cccaf67028323b0aa45375c6aff5c/runtime/lua/vim/_core/run_in_terminal.lua#L62-L64) `--clean`. can revisit that later.\n\nthanks for feedback!",
